// One pipeline cache for every platform (docs/SHADER_CACHE.md in the Port):
//
//  * Key: every pipeline is keyed by an xxh3 hash of its complete POD config
//    (shader config, vertex layout, blend/depth/cull state, sample count), per
//    shader type. Port-side custom pipelines (register_pipeline_type) use the
//    same keys and the same path.
//  * Key sets: the game names the scene (overlay) it is loading with
//    aurora_set_pipeline_scene(). Every pipeline a scene draws is recorded
//    against it, with how many frames into the scene it was first used.
//  * Persistence: the configs and scene sets live in pipeline_cache.db under
//    the cache path (files on desktop/Android, the IndexedDB-backed file
//    system on the web); the backend's compiled shader/pipeline binaries live
//    in Dawn's blob cache (dawn_cache.db, see webgpu/gpu_cache.cpp) and the
//    browser's own cache on the web.
//  * Seed: a bundled initial_pipeline_cache.db, generated by playing every
//    module (tools/generate_shader_seed.py), is merged into the local cache
//    when it changes, so a first visit to a scene prewarms too.
//  * Prewarm: when a scene starts loading, its recorded set is queued in
//    first-use order and built by background compile threads (native) or
//    asynchronously by the browser (web) while the load screen runs.
//  * Fallback: a draw whose pipeline is still missing builds it right there
//    (taking it out of the queue) and is counted as a stall in the telemetry.
//  * Safety: configs are versioned and size-checked; a crash while prewarming
//    quarantines the learned set on the next launch, and a second one turns
//    prewarm off for that launch.
namespace aurora::webgpu {
// webgpu/gpu_cache.cpp: drops Dawn's blob cache when the adapter/driver
// changed (its entries can't be used again) or it outgrew its budget.
void cache_check_identity();
} // namespace aurora::webgpu

